## Scope

This file describes the procedural route for an individual labor claim in the Kingdom: the internal grievance for disciplinary penalties, the mandatory friendly-settlement stage administered by HRSD, the labor courts of the Ministry of Justice as the forum of first instance and appeal, the twelve-month limitation and its two statutory exceptions, the prohibition on changing employment terms while a case is pending, the remedies for wage deductions and late wages, and the enforcement of settlement records, judgments and the wage clause of a documented contract. It is written for termination-review, wage-hour-qa and internal-investigation, which need to know what a claimant can do, by when, and what evidence the forum will ask for.

It does not cover: the Law of Procedure before the Sharia Courts and the labor-court circuit structure (not provided), collective disputes, the domestic-worker settlement rules (a separate HRSD instrument listed on its page), criminal complaints (harassment, human trafficking), or the Board of Grievances route for HRSD administrative penalties beyond what Reg. Art. 38 says. The friendly-settlement rules themselves were not readable and every statement about their content is model knowledge.

## Rules

Tag rules: `[settled — last confirmed YYYY-MM-DD]` only where the primary text was read on that date; `[model knowledge — verify]` for anything else, including practical-effect commentary that goes beyond the article's words.

| Article | Rule (English) | Rule (authoritative language) | Practical effect | Tag |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Law Part XIV, Arts. 210–228 (repealed) | The Commissions for Settlement of Labor Disputes (preliminary and high commissions), their jurisdiction, the labor-office friendly-settlement step (old Art. 220), the 12-month rule (old Art. 222), the arbitration clause (old Art. 224) and the litigation regulations were repealed by Royal Decree M/1 of 22/1/1435H. `boe/labor-law-ar.md` marks each of them [معدلة] and prints the old text with the repeal note. | تم إلغاء الباب الرابع عشر بموجب المرسوم الملكي (م/1) وتاريخ 22/1/1435هـ. | Do not cite Arts. 210–228 as live law. Labor claims are heard by the labor courts within the Ministry of Justice (first-instance labor courts or circuits, labor appeal circuits), which began operating in 1440H (October 2018) under the judiciary reorganisation `[model knowledge — verify]` as to the establishing instruments and the current circuit map. Old Art. 224 is not the basis of friendly settlement. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` (repeal note) |
| Law Art. 234(a) (M/14 of 1440H) — limitation | The labor courts may not hear any claim to a right under the Law or arising from an employment contract after twelve months from the end of the employment relationship, unless the claimant presents an excuse the court accepts or the defendant acknowledges the right. | لا تقبل أمام المحاكم العمالية أي دعوى تتعلق بالمطالبة بحق من الحقوق المنصوص عليها في هذا النظام أو الناشئة عن عقد العمل بعد مضي اثني عشر شهراً من تاريخ انتهاء علاقة العمل، ما لم يقدم المدعي عذراً تقبله المحكمة، أو يصدر من المدعى عليه إقرار بالحق. | The clock runs from the end of the relationship, not from the breach; claims by a serving employee (unpaid overtime, deductions) are not time-barred while employed. The two exceptions are a court-accepted excuse and the defendant's acknowledgment — an employer's final-settlement statement or Qiwa record admitting an amount can restart the claim. Whether filing a friendly-settlement request interrupts the twelve months is not in the Law `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 234(b) | Labor suits are heard expeditiously. | تنظر الدعاوى العمالية على وجه الاستعجال. | Labor cases are summary in character; expect short hearing intervals and limited adjournments `[model knowledge — verify]` as to current time-to-judgment. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 235 (M/14 of 1440H) | While a suit is pending before the labor courts the employer may not change the terms of employment in force before the proceedings began in a way that prejudices the worker's position in the suit. | لا يجوز لصاحب العمل أثناء نظر الدعوى أمام المحاكم العمالية أن يغير من شروط التشغيل التي كانت سارية قبل بدء الإجراءات، تغييراً يترتب عليه الإضرار بموقف العامل في الدعوى. | Freezes transfers, demotions and pay changes for a worker who has sued; Reg. Art. 14 Second 8(a) separately punishes an employer who prolongs the case (absent from two hearings without accepted excuse) by allowing the worker to transfer without consent. Whether the freeze covers the friendly-settlement stage is not stated `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 8 | Any condition contrary to the Law is void, and any release or settlement of the worker's rights under the Law during the currency of the contract is void, unless more beneficial to the worker. | يبطل كل شرط يخالف أحكام هذا النظام، ويبطل كل إبراء أو مصالحة عن الحقوق الناشئة للعامل بموجب هذا النظام أثناء سريان عقد العمل، ما لم يكن أكثر فائدة للعامل. | A settlement and release signed while the contract is still running is void unless it improves on the statutory floor; releases are safer once the relationship has ended, and a settlement record made before HRSD after termination is the form that is enforced `[model knowledge — verify]` as to court treatment of post-termination releases below the statutory floor. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 72 (M/44 of 1446H) and Annex 1 Art. 71 — disciplinary grievance | The worker must be notified in writing of a penalty decision (registered mail to the address on file if he refuses or is absent); he may grieve in writing to the employer's competent body within 30 days (excluding official holidays) of notification; if the grievance is rejected or not decided in writing within 15 days, he may object before the labor courts within 30 days (excluding official holidays) of the rejection or of the lapse of the 15 days, whichever is earlier. | له التظلم كتابة للجهة المختصة لدى صاحب العمل خلال (ثلاثين) يوماً - عدا أيام العطل الرسمية - من تاريخ إبلاغه بالقرار، فإن رُفض تظلمه أو لم يُبت فيه كتابة خلال (خمسة عشر) يوماً من تقديمه كان له حق الاعتراض أمام المحاكم العمالية ... خلال (ثلاثين) يوماً. | Read from the M/44 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`; the original text (15 days to the commission) precedes it. A dismissal is a "penalty" under Annex 1 Art. 58(6)–(7), so the internal grievance is available for dismissals too; a worker who skips it can still sue within Art. 234 `[model knowledge — verify]` as to whether courts treat the 30-day objection window as a bar. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` (Annex 1 Art. 71: `[authority — HRSD]`) |
| Law Art. 91(2) | Objections to a deduction for damage to the employer's equipment or products (capped at five days' wage a month) must be raised within 15 working days — by the employer from discovery of the incident, by the worker from the employer's notification — or the right lapses; if the forum finds the deduction unjustified in whole or part the employer refunds within seven days of the judgment. | يكون تظلم أي من الطرفين خلال خمسة عشر يوم عمل، وإلا سقط الحق فيه، ويبدأ موعد التظلم بالنسبة إلى صاحب العمل من تاريخ اكتشاف الواقعة، وبالنسبة إلى العامل من تاريخ إبلاغ صاحب العمل له بذلك. | The only 15-working-day limitation in the Law; the text still names "هيئة تسوية الخلافات العمالية" — now read as the labor courts. wage-hour-qa should date the employer's notification of any damage deduction. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 94 | Where an amount is deducted from wages for a reason not provided in the Law without the worker's written consent, or the employer delays wages beyond the statutory due date without legitimate cause, the worker, his representative or the director of the competent labor office may apply to the forum for an order that the employer refund the deduction or pay the late wages; the forum may fine the employer up to double the amount deducted or delayed. | إذا حسم من أجر العامل أي مبلغ لسبب غير ما هو منصوص عليه في هذا النظام بغير موافقته الكتابية، أو تأخر صاحب العمل عن أداء أجر العامل في موعد استحقاقه ... كان للعامل أو لمن يمثله أو مدير مكتب العمل المختص أن يتقدم بطلب ... يجوز للهيئة المذكورة ... أن توقع عليه غرامة لا تتجاوز ضعف ما حسم من أجر العامل أو ضعف قيمة الأجر المتأخر. | The labor-office director's standing means HRSD can bring the late-wage claim itself (the WPS route in practice) `[model knowledge — verify]`. Unamended text; the forum reference is now the labor court. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Law Art. 83(3) (M/46 of 1436H) | As an exception to the Law, the employer may sue within one year from discovering the worker's breach of a non-competition or confidentiality undertaking. | استثناء من أحكام هذا النظام، لصاحب العمل رفع دعوى خلال سنة من تاريخ اكتشاف مخالفة العامل لأي من التزاماته الواردة في هذه المادة. | The employer's non-compete claim runs from discovery, not from the end of the relationship — the one statutory departure from Art. 234 in the employer's favour. Read from the M/46 amending block in `boe/labor-law-ar.md`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` |
| Reg. Arts. 1(2), 17, 27 Third, 28(5) | Labor courts have jurisdiction over disputes under casual, seasonal and temporary contracts, training and qualification contracts, part-time and flexible-work contracts, and over work-injury compensation determinations refused by either party. | تختص المحاكم العمالية بالنظر في الخلافات التي قد تنشأ بين الطرفين في كل من عقد العمل العرضي والموسمي والمؤقت ... من عقود التدريب والتأهيل ... عن عقد العمل لبعض الوقت وعقد العمل المرن ... يحال الموضوع إلى المحاكم العمالية المختصة للفصل فيه. | Confirms that no category of worker is routed elsewhere (e.g. to the commercial courts or general courts); worker-classification disputes over "trainee" or "freelancer" status are labor-court matters. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 13.4 (unified contract) | Except for the net-wage obligation in cl. 13.3, every dispute arising from or relating to the contract, including any additional terms, is first resolved through friendly settlement; if settlement fails, jurisdiction lies with the labor courts of the Kingdom. | فإن كل نزاع أو خلاف ينشأ عن هذا العقد أو يتعلق به بأي صورة من الصور ... يتم حلّه ابتداءً من خلال التسوية الودية، وفي حال تعذر الوصول إلى تسوية، فينعقد الاختصاص بنظر النزاع للمحاكم العمالية في المملكة العربية السعودية. | The contract itself makes friendly settlement a condition precedent to suit for every Qiwa-documented worker, independent of the ministerial rules. An arbitration clause in additional terms would conflict with cl. 13.4 and be void under cl. 14.5 `[model knowledge — verify]` as to whether labor courts would honour an employment arbitration clause at all after the repeal of old Art. 224. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Friendly settlement — Ministerial Decision 91285 of 20/6/1445H | HRSD approved "Rules and Procedures Regulating Friendly Settlement of Labor Disputes" by Decision 91285 dated 20/6/1445H (page dated 22 Jumada II 1445H). Content, as understood but NOT read: a labor claim is filed electronically (through the Ministry of Justice's Najiz portal or the HRSD channel), is routed to the HRSD labor office / friendly-settlement unit, which summons the parties, attempts settlement within a fixed window of 21 working days, records any settlement in a settlement record (محضر تسوية) enforceable as an executive instrument, and, failing settlement, issues a referral (إحالة) enabling the claimant to proceed to the labor court; certain claims (e.g. claims by or against the Ministry, urgent claims) may bypass settlement. | قرار وزاري باعتماد القواعد والإجراءات المنظمة للتسوية الودية في الخلافات العمالية بالصيغة المرافقة للقرار. قرار رقم 91285 وتاريخ 20-06-1445هـ. | Only the decision number, title and date are settled (read from the HRSD page). The 21-working-day window, the filing channel, the record's enforceability, the bypass categories and the consequence of non-attendance are model knowledge and must be confirmed from the rules PDF (scanned) or from Saudi counsel before a skill relies on them. | Decision number and date: `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]`; content: `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| Annex 5 cl. 13.3 (unified contract) — executive instrument | The contract is an executive instrument (سند تنفيذي) and the Enforcement Court has jurisdiction over the employer's obligation to pay the net wage due under cl. 9.1.1.7. | يعد هذا العقد سنداً تنفيذياً، وينعقد الاختصاص لمحكمة التنفيذ فيما يلي: التزام الطرف الأول بدفع صافي الأجر المستحق الوارد في الفقرة (9.1.1.7) من البند رقم (9) من هذا العقد. | The documented net-wage line can be enforced directly before the enforcement court without a labor-court judgment, provided the platform data evidence non-payment; the route does not extend to allowances outside cl. 9.1.1, commissions, in-kind benefits, overtime, leave pay or the end-of-service award, which remain labor-court claims. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Direct wage-clause enforcement program (Qiwa–Najiz–Mudad) | As reported (not read in any source): HRSD and the Ministry of Justice recognise the wage clause of a Qiwa-documented contract as directly enforceable, with automatic verification of non-payment through a Qiwa–Najiz–Mudad link and no further documents; the program was rolled out in phases by contract type, with a third phase said to extend it to open-ended contracts from 6 August 2026. | (لم يُقرأ نص رسمي) | Consistent with Annex 5 cl. 13.3 but the phasing, the eligibility of open-ended contracts, the verification mechanics and the employer's defences (e.g. lawful deductions under Art. 92, suspension under Reg. Art. 25) are unverified. Source: `docs/amendment-watch-2026-09-04.md` lead 1.1 (law-firm note). A skill may mention the route only as a lead to confirm. | `[model knowledge — verify]` |
| Enforcement Law 1447H, Art. 7 (not yet in force) | Compulsory enforcement requires an executive instrument for a specific right due for performance; executive instruments include: (a) final judgments, orders and decisions, and judgments with immediate enforceability, of the Kingdom's courts; (b) arbitral awards per the relevant provisions; (c) settlement agreements and conciliation documents notarised under the Notarisation Law or issued by bodies authorised by law; (d) bills of exchange and promissory notes registered on the national electronic platforms; (e) cheques; (f) contracts and acknowledgments notarised under the Notarisation Law; (g) foreign judgments, awards, settlements and notarised documents per Art. 9; (h) contracts and documents given the status of executive instruments by a law or a Council of Ministers decision. | لا يجوز التنفيذ الجبري إلا بسند تنفيذي، اقتضاءً لحقٍّ معيّنٍ حالّ الأداء. والسندات التنفيذية ... هي: أ- الأحكام والأوامر والقرارات النهائية ... ج- اتفاقات التسوية ووثائق الصلح الموثّقة وفقاً لنظام التوثيق، أو التي تصدرها الجهات المخولة بذلك نظاماً ... ح- العقود والمحررات التي لها حكم السندات التنفيذية بموجب نظام أو قرار صادر من مجلس الوزراء. | Issued 20 April 2026, published 1 May 2026, in force 180 days after publication (about 28 October 2026). Until then the 1433H Enforcement Law (not provided) applies; its list of executive instruments is understood to be materially similar (judgments, awards, settlement records issued by authorised bodies, notarised documents, commercial paper, contracts given executive status by law) `[model knowledge — verify]`. Item (c) is the hook for an HRSD friendly-settlement record; item (h) is the hook for the unified contract's wage clause, if the enabling decision exists `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` (text read; not in force) |
| Enforcement Law 1447H, Arts. 36–37 (not yet in force) | For an obligation to do or refrain, failing performance within five working days of notification of the enforcement order, the court orders the use of force or the competent authority to carry out the right, and, if that fails or the obligation is personal, a travel ban and a daily fine up to SAR 10,000; after 30 working days without performance the court may, on the applicant's request, order imprisonment up to 180 days, extendable. | إذا كان محل التنفيذ فعلاً أو امتناعاً عن فعل، ولم يُنفذ المنفذ ضده التزامه خلال (خمسة) أيام عمل ... تفرض المحكمة غرامة لا تزيد على (عشرة آلاف) ريال يومياً ... فتأمر المحكمة بحبس المنفذ ضده لإجباره على التنفيذ بما لا يزيد على (مائة وثمانين) يوماً. | Relevant to reinstatement or document-return orders against an employer once the new Law is in force; money judgments follow the seizure and sale chapters (not summarised). | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]` (text read; not in force) |
| Reg. Art. 38 and Law Art. 230 — HRSD penalty decisions | Administrative penalty decisions under the Minister's table 1 may be objected to within 60 days of notification before the Ministry's objections centre (without suspending the fine), with a petitions committee above it, and challenged before the competent administrative court (Board of Grievances) under Law Art. 230(1); penalties under table 2 and permanent closure are sought by the Ministry by suit before the labor courts (Law Art. 230(4), Reg. Art. 38 Second (2)); settlement of a violation is available on application within 90 days. | يتم الاعتراض على القرار الإداري بإيقاع عقوبات مخالفات العمل خلال (ستين) يوماً من تاريخ تبليغ المخالف بالقرار الإداري ... توجيه المختصين برفع دعاوى على المخالفين أمام المحكمة المختصة (المحاكم العمالية) ... ويجوز التظلم من القرار الصادر بالعقوبة أمام المحكمة الإدارية المختصة. | Employer-side route: an HRSD fine is contested administratively, then before the administrative court, not the labor court; the labor court is the forum only when the Ministry sues for the heavier penalties. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (Law Art. 230: `[BOE — Arabic]`) |
| Annex 5 cl. 14.1 (unified contract) — notices as evidence | Notices, notifications and any act relating to the contract have legal effect only if made through the services, means or forms approved by the Portal and documented there; this applies to communications to the other party and to government or judicial bodies. | اتفق الطرفان على أن الإشعارات والإخطارات وأي تصرفات تصدر لأي غرض ... لن تكون منتجة لآثارها القانونية إلا إذا تمّت بواسطة الخدمات أو الوسائل أو النماذج التي تعتمدها المنصة لهذا الغرض ... ويسري ذلك على جميع الإشعارات ... التي يوجّهها أحد الطرفين للآخر أو للجهات الحكومية أو القضائية. | In a labor-court case the Qiwa record of termination, resignation, warnings and contract amendments is the primary evidence; paper or email notices for which a Portal service existed are contractually ineffective. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Reg. Art. 14 Second 8(a) and (c) | The Minister may approve transfer of a non-Saudi worker without the employer's consent where a case between them is pending and the employer prolongs it (absent from two hearings at one instance without an excuse the court accepts, or the court finds delay), provided the worker did not cause the delay; or where wages are unpaid for three consecutive months (application within one Hijri year from the third month's due date). | وجود دعوى بين العامل وصاحب العمل منظورة لدى إحدى الجهات القضائية، وتسبب صاحب العمل بإطالة أمد نظرها ... إذا تغيب صاحب العمل أو من يمثله عن حضور جلستين في درجة قضائية واحدة دون عذر شرعي تقبله الجهة القضائية. | A litigation-conduct sanction outside the court's own powers: an employer that stalls loses the worker. termination-review should warn clients that non-attendance has a mobility consequence. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` |
| Law Art. 234 in relation to HRSD violation complaints | The Law no longer contains a limitation for complaints about violations (old Art. 222(3), twelve months from the violation, was repealed with Part XIV); Reg. Art. 38 Second requires the penalties unit to study "مدة نظامية ضبطها" (the statutory period for recording the violation) but does not state it. | ينشئ وكيل الوزارة ... وحدة أو مركز يختص بتلقي محضر ضبط مخالفة العمل من مفتشي العمل، ودراسة مدة نظامية ضبطها، وتصنيفها. | Whether a limitation applies to HRSD's power to fine is not settled in the texts read `[model knowledge — verify]`. | `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [authority — HRSD]` (as to what the text does and does not say) |

## Open questions for a local practitioner

- The friendly-settlement rules (Decision 91285 of 20/6/1445H) themselves: the filing channel (Najiz versus an HRSD portal), the 21-working-day window and whether it is extendable, what happens on non-attendance by either party, whether the settlement record is issued by an "authorised body" for Enforcement Law purposes, whether filing interrupts the Art. 234 twelve months, and which claims bypass settlement. The PDF provided is a scanned image; a text copy is needed.
- Labor-court structure and appeal: the instruments establishing the labor courts and labor appeal circuits, the appeal window, and whether Supreme Court review is available on labor matters (nothing in the sources read).
- Employment arbitration after the repeal of old Art. 224: whether an arbitration clause in the additional terms of a Qiwa contract is enforceable or void under Annex 5 cl. 14.5 and Art. 8.
- Direct enforcement of the wage clause: the enabling instrument (a Council of Ministers decision under Enforcement Law item (h), a ministerial framework, or the contract clause alone), the phasing by contract type, the reported 6 August 2026 extension to open-ended contracts, and the employer's procedural defences.
- The 1433H Enforcement Law (still in force until about 28 October 2026): confirm its executive-instruments list matches the summary above and whether an HRSD settlement record is enforced directly or needs court endorsement.
- Whether Art. 235's freeze on employment terms begins at the friendly-settlement filing or only at the court filing.
- Whether the Art. 72 30-day objection window is treated by the labor courts as a bar to a later Art. 234 claim challenging a dismissal.
- Any limitation on HRSD's power to record and fine violations after the repeal of old Art. 222(3).

## How skills should use this file

- **termination-review** loads this file at the exposure-and-timeline step and must cite Law Art. 234(a) (twelve months from the end of the relationship, two exceptions), Art. 235 (no change of terms during suit), Art. 72 / Annex 1 Art. 71 (30-15-30 grievance ladder for disciplinary dismissals), Annex 5 cl. 13.4 (friendly settlement as a condition precedent), Annex 5 cl. 14.1 (Qiwa records as the effective notices), Reg. Art. 14 Second 8(a) (mobility sanction for stalling), and Art. 8 (releases during the contract void). Any statement about the 21-working-day settlement window or the settlement record's enforceability must carry `[model knowledge — verify]`.
- **wage-hour-qa** loads at the remedy step and must cite Art. 94 (refund order and fine up to double; labor-office director's standing), Art. 91(2) (15 working days for damage-deduction objections), Annex 5 cl. 13.3 (net wage as executive instrument), and must present the Qiwa–Najiz–Mudad direct-enforcement route only as `[model knowledge — verify]`.
- **internal-investigation** loads at the outcome step and must apply Art. 72 timing to the penalty notice (written notice, registered mail fallback, 30-day grievance, 15-day decision) so that the file supports the later court stage, and must note Art. 235 once a claim is filed.
- **hiring-review** and **policy-drafting** load when drafting dispute or arbitration clauses and must cite Annex 5 cls. 13.3–13.4 and 14.5 and Art. 8 to reject arbitration or foreign-forum clauses in employment contracts.
- **Computed dates:** limitation deadline = end-of-relationship date + 12 months (Gregorian if the contract elects the Gregorian calendar under Annex 5 cl. 14.6, otherwise Hijri per Law Art. 10), tagged `[settled — last confirmed 2026-09-04] [BOE — Arabic]`; grievance deadlines = notification + 30 days excluding official holidays, then +15 days, then +30 days excluding official holidays, same tag; any friendly-settlement window computed from the 21-working-day figure must be tagged `[model knowledge — verify]`.
- **Stop rule:** if a skill needs the content of the friendly-settlement rules, the labor-court appeal mechanics, the 1433H Enforcement Law text, or the direct wage-enforcement program terms — all `[model knowledge — verify]` or absent here — it must say so and stop or flag for Saudi counsel; it must not supply them from memory. Where the task or a user cites "Art. 220/222/224" for friendly settlement, limitation or arbitration, the skill must point out that Part XIV is repealed and cite Arts. 234–235 and Annex 5 cl. 13 instead.

